 this instance: 2 of 3. Reply with a corrected program and {\"action\": \"submit\"}, or with {\"action\": \"request_demos\"}.","reply":"```python\ndef transform(grid):\n    h, w = len(grid), len(grid[0])\n    from collections import Counter\n    base = Counter(v for row in grid for v in row).most_common(1)[0][0]\n\n    # Find the repeating horizontal and vertical grid-line positions.\n    hr = [r for r in range(h) if sum(v != base for v in grid[r]) > w // 3]\n    vc = [c for c in range(w) if sum(grid[r][c] != base for r in range(h)) > h // 3]\n\n    def regular_positions(vals):\n        if len(vals) < 2:\n            return vals\n        step = min(b-a for a, b in zip(vals, vals[1:]))\n        return [p for p in vals if (p-vals[0]) % step == 0]\n\n    hr, vc = regular_positions(hr), regular_positions(vc)\n    # Keep the first marker positions that fit the compact output lattice.\n    out_h = max(1, len(hr)-1)\n    out_w = max(1, len(vc)-1)\n    out = [[base for _ in range(out_w)] for _ in range(out_h)]\n    for i, r in enumerate(hr[:out_h]):\n        for j, c in enumerate(vc[:out_w]):\n            if grid[r][c] != base:\n                out[i][j] = grid[r][c]\n    return out\n```\n{\"action\":\"submit\"}","steps":[],"action":{"type":"submit"}},{"step":78,"kind":"reprompt","phase":"act","t0":1793589940.133,"t1":1793589950.733,"alias":"task-4bcb43b3","message":"Your program was checked on earlier pair 1 at no cost and its output is wrong. It gave\n5 5 4 4 4 1 1\n5 5 4 4 4 1 1\n1 1 0 0 4 4 4\n1 1 0 0 0 9 9\nwhere the pair's output is\n5 8 8 8 8 1\n8 8 8 8 8 8\n1 8 0 8 8 8\n8 8 8 0 8 9\nFailed checks in this instance: 3 of 3. Reply with a corrected program and {\"action\": \"submit\"}, or with {\"action\": \"request_demos\"}.","reply":"```python\ndef transform(grid):\n    h, w = len(grid), len(grid[0])\n\n    # The repeated cell interiors have one common color; grid lines have another.\n    from collections import Counter\n    counts = Counter(v for row in grid for v in row)\n    interior = counts.most_common(1)[0][0]\n\n    # Identify the periodic horizontal and vertical separator lines by their\n    # unusually high frequency of colors other than the interior color.\n    row_scores = [sum(v != interior for v in row) for row in grid]\n    col_scores = [sum(grid[r][c] != interior for r in range(h)) for c in range(w)]\n    rlines = [r for r, s in enumerate(row_scores) if s > w * 0.6]\n    clines = [c for c, s in enumerate(col_scores) if s > h * 0.6]\n\n    # Keep the regularly spaced separator positions.\n    def periodic_positions(pos):\n        if len(pos) < 2:\n            return pos\n        step = min(b - a for a, b in zip(pos, pos[1:]))\n        return [p for p in pos if (p - pos[0]) % step == 0]\n\n    rlines = periodic_positions(rlines)\n    clines = periodic_positions(clines)\n    if len(rlines) < 2 or len(clines) < 2:\n        return [[interior]]\n\n    out = [[interior for _ in range(len(clines) - 1)]\n           for _ in range(len(rlines) - 1)]\n    for i, r in enumerate(rlines[:-1]):\n        for j, c in enumerate(clines[:-1]):\n            v = grid[r][c]\n            if v != interior:\n                out[i][j] = v\n    return out\n```\n{\"action\":\"submit\"}","steps":[],"action":{"type":"submit","correct":false,"valid":true}},{"step":78,"kind":"observation","phase":"act","t0":1793589950.845,"t1":1793589956.435,"alias":"task-4bcb43b3","message":"Feedback since your last action:\nYour submission was INCORRECT. Wrong attempts so far: 1.\n\nSame instance. Task id: task-4bcb43b3\nTest input (27x22):\n7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3\n4 7 7 7 7 4 7 7 7 7 6 7 7 7 7 6 7 7 7 7 6 7\n7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3\n7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3\n7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3\n4 7 7 7 7 4 7 7 7 7 6 7 7 7 7 6 7 7 7 7 6 7\n7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3\n7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3\n7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3 3 3 3 7 3\n6 7 7 7 7 6 7 7 7 7 7 7